   "body": "The diminutive <em>misellam</em> (\"poor little [me]\") is a touch of self-pity that also flatters the listening sister. Apuleius loves such affectionate diminutives; here it underscores Psyche’s helplessness — and, to the reader, her dangerous naivety.",
